  "specId": "80341e7f-flow-help-contract",
  "issue": 521,
  "request": "Goal: Make the public sennel flow help output match the actual argument contract and render group subcommands consistently.\n\nScope: Follow Issue #521 restart contract dated 2026-09-24 as the authority for the initial Draft and Spec; it supersedes historical counts and wording. Re-enumerate FLOW_COMMANDS from source. Extend CommandDefinition and FLOW_COMMANDS with explicit option and subcommand-row models, project parser and help from the same authority, derive group options from all direct child leaves, and share the row renderer across every documented entry point. Preserve flow query as its separate parser exception and test it independently. Inventory each leaf input against its existing validator and owner, including path, value, size, state-dependent, guard, runtime, rejection-order, and exit-code contracts. Reuse existing authorities and behavior; do not invent blanket admission validation or new limits. Add registry/integration coverage for every routed leaf and focused CLI E2E coverage for render paths and representative behavior. Keep command execution semantics, guards, runtime directory policy, query behavior, and rejection lifecycle intact. The stopped flow recovery is separate scope.\n\nDescription: Correct missing or misleading flow options, invalid group options, broken subcommand spacing, and declaration-order output. The Issue body contains the detailed acceptance criteria and contract inventory; carry them into the initial Draft and Spec.",
